<div id="S4.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">The RGO potential has Hessian between
<math id="S4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\kappa^{-1}+\eta^{-1})\,I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\kappa^{-1}+\eta^{-1})\,I</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1+\eta^{-1})\,I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1+\eta^{-1})\,I</annotation></semantics></math>. The
Brascamp–Lieb covariance inequality <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>]</cite> gives</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Cov}(X\mid Y=y)\preceq(\kappa^{-1}+\eta^{-1})^{-1}I\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Cov}(X\mid Y=y)\preceq(\kappa^{-1}+\eta^{-1})^{-1}I\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">For the reverse bound, the
Cramér–Rao inequality (see, e.g., <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>, Theorem 3.5.8]</cite>) gives</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Cov}(X\mid Y=y)\succeq(1+\eta^{-1})^{-1}I\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪰</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Cov}(X\mid Y=y)\succeq(1+\eta^{-1})^{-1}I\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Substitute both bounds in
(<a href="#S4.E1" title="Equation 4.1 ‣ 4.1 Setup and smoothing estimates ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>